Z||000000||perks88gt||04-30-2001||05:17 PM||||Im looking for a short shifter for my fiero?  Im not sure which company to buy from.  I know the fiero store sells one, and Rodney Dickman, both of whom I have had bad experiences.  Is there anyone else?  Do you know if there product is good?||||reg||5
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||04-30-2001||05:28 PM||||talk to DXR_DAD, he made his own. that might give you some ideas. But if you want to buy one, then I do recommend Rodney Dickman.. Tom McElroy used to sell them as well, and there's a couple of other people on the forum who do this mod. Check around, you'll find a good deal!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com/dxr/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com/dxr/</A>  - DXR_DAD's site<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||14
Z||000002||85Josh||04-30-2001||05:50 PM||||I just got a short, straight shifter from Randy Agee, <A HREF="http://fierozone.tripod.com" TARGET=_blank>http://fierozone.tripod.com</A>  , and a shift boot from Rodney. They were both at the swap meet at Ed Parks place. I installed them in the parking lot, and loved the feel on my way home.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||05-01-2001||12:29 AM||||I just got the sport shifter from Rodney at the Alabama meet, and I think it's a good improvement.  It has a much more positive feel, which I like the most.  It also included a much smaller shift ball (mine had a huge round black one), the leather boot, and the stainless shaft.  Oh, and it points straight up in neutral, I like that too.  I think cost is a few bucks too high, but overall I'm glad I got it.  It's easy enough to make your own if you want to go to the trouble, but it is very very easy to install after you've bought one.  Instant gratification, sweet!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 05-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever2||05-01-2001||02:17 AM||||I recently purchased one from V8fieroGT here on the Forum.  Was very inexpensive, got exactly what I asked for, and he contacted me often to follow up on shipping and to see how I liked it.  And I like it a lot!   Big thumbs up.  I don't see how he made any profit from it, but it's a great service to us.<P>||||reg||14
Z||000005||PKFieroGT||05-01-2001||09:07 AM||||Short shifters are awesome...if you know someone who can weld,or you can weld yourself, you can make your own. Go to a scrap yard and pick up a shifter from another GM car that has the straight short shift that's obout 3-4 inches long, grind out the welds that hold it in place, and do the same to the Fiero shifter. Then just weld the shorter piece to your original shifter. simple really...<BR>BTW see my post regarding the Short shifter, or if you have any more ??? E-mail me.<P>Petri||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tryxalon||05-01-2001||09:11 PM||||Just because I have a contrary opinion   ---<P>I like the standard Shifter. The throw and feel are "right". <P>A shorter shifter would be harder to move and put into the gears. The reach of the shifter feels "right" - a shorter shifter would require more effort, and would feel wrong ... like something stops your "throw" before it should. <P>If I wanted less effort or throw I'd get an automatic.<P><BR>  Or a ricer.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||2xsess||05-01-2001||11:30 PM||||<B>Just because I have a contrary opinion ---<BR>I like the standard Shifter. The throw and feel are "right". <P><BR>If I wanted less effort or throw I'd get an automatic.<P><BR>Or a ricer. </B><BR>Might want to watch what you imply there buddy. You'll soon find out that most of us members have short shifters and if you'd ever driven one with a short shifter you see why.<P>Anyways. FieroDave was also selling short shifters, I have one, good quality. Only $40 too!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>  <B>*For Sale*<BR>        $2000obo</B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">        <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Eric||05-02-2001||12:18 AM||||Maybe he's just got really short girly arms.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I bought Rodney's shifter a couple years ago.  The quality is very good, and, I believe, the boot alone is worth every bit of the price he wants.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Cheever2||05-02-2001||02:08 AM||||*** CHEEVER2'S FIRST DOUBLE POST ***<P>Took me 1,471 posts, but I finally did it!<P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 05-02-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000010||Cheever2||05-02-2001||02:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>a shorter shifter would require more effort<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I know why you say that, and I wondered if that would happen, but you are simply incorrect.  Maybe it defies logic, but there is no more effort with mine.<P>You are certainly entitled to your opinion.  But you might not understand until you try it for yourself... don't even use your own, send out a shifter from a salvage to my man V8fieroGT (Daniel).  They are easy as pie to install (if I can do it you can), but if you don't like it then swap it back and sell it to someone else.  There will be plenty of takers.<BR> <BR>I'm tellin ya, it's like it shoulda been that way from the factory.  See for yourself.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000011||TOM||05-02-2001||02:19 AM||||$35 Including shiiping. Email me tmc87@msn.com Dave is not selling them anymore. I ought to know.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Tryxalon||05-02-2001||05:51 PM||||Okay guys, you convinced me to visit the boneyard this weekend. <P> After all there are all kinds of directions on how to make the shifter shorter  <A HREF="http://fierozone.tripod.com/weekend/shifter/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fierozone.tripod.com/weekend/shifter/index.html</A>  <P>... Why did you have to use logic?? Flames and Demagogery I can either ignore or counter, but logic and "try it yourself" engage my Curiosity. <P>And that is dangerous!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>(and I can't help but laugh at the comment about "short girly arms" --- we orangatangs (36 inch reach) are easily amused.)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by Tryxalon (edited 05-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||banditbalz||05-02-2001||06:47 PM||||I also enjoy the feel of the standard shifter. Wanted to see what all the  fuss was about short shifters, so i went to the wrecking yard and pulled one from a 2m4. It sits about 1.5" lower now. Still feels good and I was surprised that it did not take any more effort to shift. A good compromize.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/</A> <P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||14
Z||000014||KissMySSFiero||05-02-2001||08:54 PM||||i think banditbalz has an 84 shifter.  tahts what ive got too.  much shorter than the other years but looks stock.  i have a half a dozen or so shifters here.  and theyre a dime a dozen in the yards.  most of them are from 84's since that was the most produced year.  i think.  so its really not worth it to sell them.  i also have an 85 shifter.  its taller than an 84 by about an inch.  but it has a straight shaft about 4 or 5 inches that would be perfect to cut and make a short shifter and keep the stock knob for the look.  maybe sunday i can get in the garage and see what i can make up.  =Þ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Tryxalon||05-13-2001||11:07 AM||||Well guys, went to the bone yard last weekend and found an 84 shifter, modified it and put it in my 85 SE Duke w/Isuzu tranny. You challenged me to try it. <P>I just got through putting my old shifter back in mine and installing the shortened shifter in an 84 that a girl I work with drives. Took an entire hour and 45 minutes for two dis-installs, two installs and adjustments. <P>With her short girly arms, (she is 5'4") She LOVES it!!! Says she is less worried about banging her nails on something.  <P>I hated it, as with my long ass gorilla arms (well over 6' tall) I was always slamming it against the shift stops and had to readjust my cables three times during the one week!!  <P>However, I must admit it did not require any more effort .. and also I must admit that one COULD get used to it, but I like the original feel.<P>But then, no accounting for taste!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000016||sjp777||05-13-2001||12:21 PM||||Do it yourself. Here's how:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/short_shifter_conversion.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/short_shifter_conversion.htm</A> <P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
